{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-psa-59-1","title":"Psalms 59:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":59,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":59,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 David prays to be delivered from his enemies. 6 He complains of their cruelty. 8 He trusts in God. 11 He prays against them. 16 He praises God.</p>\n<p>A.M. 2942. B.C. 1062. (Title.) {Al-tas-chith.} or,destroy not. A golden Psalm. 57:1; 58:1; *titles Michtam.The seven poems of the celebrated Arabian poets who flourished before the time of Mohammed, called {Mo�llakat,} from being suspended on the walls of the temple of Mecca, were also called {Modhabat,} \"golden,\" because they were written in letters of gold on the papyrus; and probably this is another reason why the six poems of David were called golden.</p>\n<p>when. Jud 16:2,3; 1Sa 19:11-24; 2Co 11:32,33 Deliver. 7:1,2; 18:48; 71:4; 143:12; Lu 1:74,75; 2Ti 4:17,18 defend me. Heb. set me on high. 12:5; 91:14; Isa 33:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-59-2","title":"Psalms 59:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":59,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":59,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>save. 26:9; 27:2; 55:23; 139:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-59-3","title":"Psalms 59:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":59,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":59,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>they. 10:9,10; 37:32,33; 38:12; 56:6; 1Sa 19:1; Pr 12:6; Mic 7:2; Ac 23:21 the mighty. 2:2; Ac 4:26,27 not. 7:3-6; 69:4; 1Sa 24:11,17; 26:18; Joh 15:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-59-4","title":"Psalms 59:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":59,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":59,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>run. 1Sa 19:12-24; Pr 1:16; Isa 59:7; Ac 23:15; Ro 3:15 awake. 5:6; 35:23; 44:23; Isa 51:9 help me. Heb. meet me.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-59-5","title":"Psalms 59:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":59,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":59,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>the God. Ge 33:20; Ex 3:15 visit. Ex 20:5 the heathen. 9:15; 54:3; Isa 1:10; Am 9:7; Ro 2:28,29; 9:6 be not. 7:12,13; 55:15; Isa 27:11; Eze 18:27,28; Jas 2:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-59-6","title":"Psalms 59:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":59,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":59,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>14; 1Sa 19:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-59-7","title":"Psalms 59:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":59,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":59,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>belch. Pr 15:2; *marg: Mt 12:34 swords. 55:21; 57:4; 64:3-5; 109:2,3; Pr 12:18 who. 10:11,13; 73:11; 94:7-9; Job 22:12,13; Jer 33:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-59-8","title":"Psalms 59:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":59,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":59,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Thou. 2:4; 37:13; 1Sa 19:15,16; Pr 1:26 heathen. 5; Mt 18:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-59-9","title":"Psalms 59:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":59,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":59,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>his strength.Instead of {�zzo,} \"his strength,\" fourteen MSS., read {�zzee,} \"my strength.\" \"O my strength, I will wait upon thee.\"</p>\n<p>18:1,1,2; 27:1,14; 46:1; 62:5,6,11; Isa 12:2; 26:3,4; 40:31; Mt 6:13 God. 17; 62:2 defence. Heb. high place. 9:9; 20:1; 46:7; *marg: Isa 58:14; Hab 3:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-59-10","title":"Psalms 59:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":59,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":59,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>The God. 17; 2Co 1:3; Eph 2:4,5; 1Pe 5:10 prevent. 21:3; 79:8; Isa 65:24; 1Th 4:15 let. 54:7; 91:8; 92:11; 112:8; 1Sa 26:10; 2Sa 1:11,12,17; Jer 17:16 Lu 19:41-44; Ro 10:2,3 enemies. Heb. observers. 5:8; 54:5; *marg: 56:2,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-59-11","title":"Psalms 59:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":59,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":59,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>Slay. Ge 4:12-15; Jud 1:6,7; Ec 9:5; Eze 12:15,16; 14:22,23; Re 9:6 scatter. 44:11; 52:5; Le 26:33; De 4:27; 28:64; 30:3,4; Eze 12:15; Lu 1:51,52 Lu 21:21 bring. Job 40:12 our shield. 3:3; 84:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-59-12","title":"Psalms 59:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":59,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":59,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>For the. 64:7,8; 79:12; 120:3,4; 140:9,10; Pr 12:13; 18:7; Mt 12:36,37 Mt 27:25,63 taken. 10:2; Pr 6:2; 11:6 cursing. 109:17,18; Ho 4:2; Lu 23:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-59-13","title":"Psalms 59:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":59,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":59,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Consume. 11; 7:9; Nu 14:34,35; 32:13; De 2:14-16; 7:22,23 and let. 46:10,11; 83:18; 135:5,6; 1Sa 17:46,47; 1Ki 18:36,37; 2Ki 19:19 Isa 54:5; Eze 38:23; 39:7; Da 4:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-59-14","title":"Psalms 59:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":59,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":59,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>at evening. 6; 22:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-59-15","title":"Psalms 59:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":59,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":59,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>wander. 109:10; Job 15:23; 30:1-7; Isa 8:21 for meat. Heb. to eat. De 28:48,53-58; 2Ki 6:25-29; La 4:4,5,9,10; 5:9; Mt 24:7,8 grudge, etc. or, if they be not satisfied, then they willstay all night. if. Isa 56:11; Mic 3:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-59-16","title":"Psalms 59:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":59,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":59,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>But. 9,10; 21:13; 106:8; 145:11; Ex 15:6; Job 37:23 sing aloud. 31:7; 36:5; 86:13; 89:1; 101:1; Ro 15:9; Eph 1:6,7 morning. 5:3; 30:5; 143:8; 1Sa 19:11,12 for thou. 4:1; 61:2,3; 1Sa 17:37; 2Co 1:10; Eph 3:20 day. 77:2; 116:1-5; 138:7; Jer 30:7; Heb 5:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-59-17","title":"Psalms 59:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":59,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":59,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>O my. 18:1; 46:1 for. 9,10</p>"}]}